<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for May 2.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for May 2.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the transport and pipeline arm of BG plc, announced on Thursday the following forecasts and data for UK gas consumption in the period April 30 to May 2.</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 30 (actual) 175 mcm, 41 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 1 (forecast) 158 mcm, 37 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 2 (forecast) 151 mcm, 35 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 30 (actual) 13.3 Celsius, SNT 11.2 Celsius</p>
<p>May 1 (forecast) 15.8 Celsius, SNT 11.3 Celsius</p>
<p>May 2 (forecast) 15.9 Celsius, SNT 11.5 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Thursday, with none expected on Friday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
